{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"e5a8e849710c4282","name":"card_unit_26th_infantry_regiment","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/USA/Legions/units/card_unit_26th_infantry_regiment","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"26th INFANTRY REGIMENT","text":"Has +2 attack for each adjacent unit.","flavorText":"The 26th Infantry Regiment, nicknamed “Blue Spaders”, was formed in 1901 and is a unit of the US Army.  During WWII the regiment was assigned to the 1st Infantry Division, and in 1942 they participated in the first US led amphibious assault in North Africa and saw some heavy fighting at the Battle of Kasserine Pass, which was a series of battles during the Tunisian Campaign. The regiment would later participate in the Amphibious Battle of Gela, which was during the Allied invasion of Sicily, and in 1944 they landed at Omaha Beach in Normandy during D-Day. In 1944 the regiment participated in the Battle of Aachen, which became the first German city to fall into Allied hands. That same year the 26th defended against German attacks at Elsenborn Ridge during the Battle of the Bulge. The regiment ended the war in Czechoslovakia, but would later do occupation duties in Germany and serve as guards at the Nuremberg Trials.","faction":"USA","type":"infantry","rarity":"Common","cost":4,"operationCost":1,"attack":4,"defense":4},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_unit_26th_infantry_regiment","title":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_unit_26th_infantry_regiment_title","SourceString":"26th INFANTRY REGIMENT","LocalizedString":"26th INFANTRY REGIMENT"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::infantry","attack":4,"defense":4,"range":1,"faction":"EFactionEnum::USA","kredits":4,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_unit_26th_infantry_regiment_text","SourceString":"Has +2 attack for each adjacent unit.","LocalizedString":"Has +2 attack for each adjacent unit."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_unit_26th_infantry_regiment_history","SourceString":"The 26th Infantry Regiment, nicknamed “Blue Spaders”, was formed in 1901 and is a unit of the US Army.  During WWII the regiment was assigned to the 1st Infantry Division, and in 1942 they participated in the first US led amphibious assault in North Africa and saw some heavy fighting at the Battle of Kasserine Pass, which was a series of battles during the Tunisian Campaign. The regiment would later participate in the Amphibious Battle of Gela, which was during the Allied invasion of Sicily, and in 1944 they landed at Omaha Beach in Normandy during D-Day. In 1944 the regiment participated in the Battle of Aachen, which became the first German city to fall into Allied hands. That same year the 26th defended against German attacks at Elsenborn Ridge during the Battle of the Bulge. The regiment ended the war in Czechoslovakia, but would later do occupation duties in Germany and serve as guards at the Nuremberg Trials.","LocalizedString":"The 26th Infantry Regiment, nicknamed “Blue Spaders”, was formed in 1901 and is a unit of the US Army.  During WWII the regiment was assigned to the 1st Infantry Division, and in 1942 they participated in the first US led amphibious assault in North Africa and saw some heavy fighting at the Battle of Kasserine Pass, which was a series of battles during the Tunisian Campaign. The regiment would later participate in the Amphibious Battle of Gela, which was during the Allied invasion of Sicily, and in 1944 they landed at Omaha Beach in Normandy during D-Day. In 1944 the regiment participated in the Battle of Aachen, which became the first German city to fall into Allied hands. That same year the 26th defended against German attacks at Elsenborn Ridge during the Battle of the Bulge. The regiment ended the war in Czechoslovakia, but would later do occupation duties in Germany and serve as guards at the Nuremberg Trials."},"operationCost":1,"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Common","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::Legions","isReserved":true,"showBoostIcon":true,"